          "text": "The pattern is most consistent with an **orthorhombically distorted TiNiSi-type structure**, space group **Pnma (No. 62)**, with four AlGeMo formula units per cell. The splitting near 39\u201340\u00b0 and the number of higher-angle reflections favor this model over the related hexagonal ZrNiAl-type aristotype.\n\nThe lattice and coordinates below are powder-derived/prototype-constrained estimates; a full Rietveld refinement would be needed for precise positional parameters.\n\n### Primary structure: orthorhombic TiNiSi type\n\n```cif\ndata_AlGeMo_primary\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder indexing and TiNiSi-type prototype fit'\n_chemical_name_common               'aluminium germanium molybdenum'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Al Ge Mo'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'AlGeMo'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M      'P n m a'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number         62\n\n_cell_length_a                      6.844\n_cell_length_b                      4.201\n_cell_length_c                      7.769\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nAl1 Al 4 c 0.1780 0.2500 0.5790 1.0\nMo1 Mo 4 c 0.0370 0.2500 0.1880 1.0\nGe1 Ge 4 c 0.2890 0.2500 0.8900 1.0\n```\n\n### Surviving higher-symmetry alternative: hexagonal ZrNiAl type\n\nA related **P-62m** model accounts for the main peak sequence but does not naturally reproduce the observed splitting as well as the orthorhombic model.\n\n```cif\ndata_AlGeMo_hexagonal_alternative\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder indexing and ZrNiAl-type prototype fit'\n_chemical_name_common          